      "sequence_position": 13,
      "problem": "If $r=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $s=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$, then $r\\cdot s=$",
      "worked_solution": "To compute the dot product, we add up the products of corresponding components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot s & ={r}_{1}\\cdot {s}_{1}+{r}_{2}\\cdot {s}_{2}+{r}_{3}\\cdot {s}_{3}+{r}_{4}\\cdot {s}_{4}+{r}_{5}\\cdot {s}_{5} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 3+(-1)\\cdot (-4)+3\\cdot 1+5\\cdot 1+2\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =3+4+3+5-4 \\\\  & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$",
